<!DOCTYPE suzuki [
<!ENTITY % sdatacharaents SYSTEM "..\config8\sdatacharaents.txt">
%sdatacharaents;
]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "1D">
<servcat sctnbr = "01" scnbr = "04">
<configtype typenbr = "1">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1416036" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Camshaft Removal and Installation
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1416035">Camshaft Components:K14C</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1416036001">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove timing chain. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1416033"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove vacuum pump. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1416008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove CMP sensor, if necessary. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1316020"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove high pressure fuel pump. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1716010"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove thermostat case (1) with thermostat and O-rings (2) from cylinder head.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140206.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "61.162mm" ver = "01" gw = "197" gh = "157"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
With hexagonal section of intake camshaft held stationary with spanner or adjustable wrench (1), remove VVT actuator bolt (2) and remove VVT actuator (3).
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Apply the same procedure to remove exhaust camshaft timing sprocket (4).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAA0A142006.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "63.460mm" ver = "01" gw = "216" gh = "163"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove dowel pins (1) from intake camshaft and exhaust camshaft.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140208.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "55.523mm" ver = "01" gw = "185" gh = "141"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Loosen camshaft housing bolts No.1, No.2 and camshaft intake rear housing bolts in numerical order (“1” – “23”) evenly and gradually.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140209.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "60.283mm" ver = "01" gw = "238" gh = "154"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove camshaft front upper housing (1), camshaft housings (2) and camshaft intake rear housing (3).
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove intake camshaft (4) and exhaust camshaft (5).
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove camshaft front lower housing (6).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAA0A142007.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "57.355mm" ver = "01" gw = "202" gh = "146"/>
</figure>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1416036002">
<title>
Installation
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1416037">Camshaft and VVT Actuator Inspection:K14C</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Before installing camshafts to the cylinder head, turn crankshaft counterclockwise and position the key (1) within an angle of 30&#176; – 90&#176; from TDC as shown in figure and keep the valves from coming in contact with the piston.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "I7V20A141058.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "37.283mm" ver = "01" gw = "129" gh = "89"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
“a”:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
30&#176;
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
“b”:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
90&#176;
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that all dowel pins are installed to cylinder head and camshaft front lower housing.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Fit camshaft front lower housing (1) into cylinder head.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply engine oil to bearing portions of camshaft front lower housing and cylinder head.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set intake camshaft (2) and exhaust camshaft (3) on cylinder head, and apply engine oil to sliding surfaces.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAA0A142008.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "63.992mm" ver = "01" gw = "181" gh = "165"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set camshaft housings No.2 – 5 (1) to specified places as indicated by alphabet (2), number (3) and arrow mark (4) on each camshaft housing.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140102.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "35.961mm" ver = "01" gw = "66" gh = "85"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.968in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
2.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
I: Intake camshaft housing
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
E: Exhaust camshaft housing
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
3.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position from timing chain side
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
4.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Point arrow to timing chain side
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Clean mating surface of camshaft intake rear housing and cylinder head.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply sealant “A” to mating surface of camshaft intake rear housing as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
<materials>
<materialitem name = "SUZUKI Bond No.1217G" id = "M1D103" uid = "-491504098">
<m-part>
“A”
</m-part>
<m-desc>
Sealant
</m-desc>
<m-number>
99000–31260
</m-number>
<m-name>
SUZUKI Bond No.1217G
</m-name>
</materialitem>
</materials>
<spec>
<title>
Sealant bead size for camshaft intake rear housing
</title>
<ptxt>
Width “a”: 3 mm (0.12 in.)
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Height “b”: 2 mm (0.08 in.)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140212.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "49.682mm" ver = "01" gw = "139" gh = "124"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Fit camshaft intake rear housing (1) on cylinder head and tighten the housing bolts until the housing is positioned by dowel pins.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Fit camshaft front upper housing (2) to cylinder head.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAA0A142009.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "57.355mm" ver = "01" gw = "195" gh = "146"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Tighten camshaft housing bolts according to the following procedure.
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Tighten camshaft housing bolts No.1, No.2 and camshaft intake rear housing bolts to 5.0 N&#183;m (0.51 kgf-m, 4.0 lbf-ft) in numerical order (“1” – “23”) evenly and gradually.
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
In the same manner as in Step a), tighten them to 8.0 N&#183;m (0.82 kgf-m, 6.0 lbf-ft).
</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
In the same manner as in Step b), tighten them to 11 N&#183;m (1.1 kgf-m, 8.5 lbf-ft).
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D125">
<t-part>
Camshaft housing bolt No.1*
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-note>
5.0 N&#183;m &#8594; 8.0 N&#183;m &#8594; 11 N&#183;m (0.51 kgf-m &#8594; 0.82 kgf-m &#8594; 1.1 kgf-m, 4.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 6.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 8.5 lbf-ft)
</t-note>
</torqueitem>
<torqueitem id = "T1D126">
<t-part>
Camshaft housing bolt No.2*
</t-part>
<t-part1>
b
</t-part1>
<t-note>
5.0 N&#183;m &#8594; 8.0 N&#183;m &#8594; 11 N&#183;m (0.51 kgf-m &#8594; 0.82 kgf-m &#8594; 1.1 kgf-m, 4.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 6.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 8.5 lbf-ft)
</t-note>
</torqueitem>
<torqueitem id = "T1D127">
<t-part>
Camshaft intake rear housing bolt*
</t-part>
<t-part1>
c
</t-part1>
<t-note>
5.0 N&#183;m &#8594; 8.0 N&#183;m &#8594; 11 N&#183;m (0.51 kgf-m &#8594; 0.82 kgf-m &#8594; 1.1 kgf-m, 4.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 6.0 lbf-ft &#8594; 8.5 lbf-ft)
</t-note>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140214.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "68.397mm" ver = "02" gw = "240" gh = "177"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Wipe off excessive sealant squeezed out from camshaft intake rear housing at the rear end and clean mating surface for thermostat case.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install dowel pins (1) from intake camshaft and exhaust camshaft.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140208.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "55.523mm" ver = "01" gw = "185" gh = "141"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
With hexagonal section of intake camshaft held stationary with spanner or adjustable wrench (1), tighten VVT actuator bolt (2) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Apply the same procedure to install exhaust camshaft timing sprocket (3).
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D128">
<t-part>
VVT actuator bolt
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
60
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
6.1
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
44.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
<torqueitem id = "T1D129">
<t-part>
Exhaust camshaft timing sprocket bolt
</t-part>
<t-part1>
b
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
60
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
6.1
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
44.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGAA0A142010.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "67.291mm" ver = "01" gw = "211" gh = "174"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check stud bolts and dowel pins for thermostat case are installed to cylinder head.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Apply sealant “A” to the mating surface as shown.
</ptxt>
<materials>
<materialitem name = "SUZUKI Bond No.1217G" id = "M1D104" uid = "-491504098">
<m-part>
“A”
</m-part>
<m-desc>
Sealant
</m-desc>
<m-number>
99000–31260
</m-number>
<m-name>
SUZUKI Bond No.1217G
</m-name>
</materialitem>
</materials>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140216.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "53.497mm" ver = "01" gw = "193" gh = "135"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Clean mating surface of thermostat case (1), fit new O-rings (2) to thermostat case and install it to cylinder head with thermostat.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Tighten thermostat case nuts (3) to specified torque.
</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem id = "T1D130">
<t-part>
Thermostat case nut
</t-part>
<t-part1>
a
</t-part1>
<t-value1>
25
</t-value1>
<t-value2>
2.5
</t-value2>
<t-value3>
18.5
</t-value3>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140217.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "61.162mm" ver = "01" gw = "216" gh = "157"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install high pressure fuel pump. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1716010"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install CMP sensor, if removed. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1316020"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install vacuum pump. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1416008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install timing chain. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1416033"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
</servinfo>
</servinfotype>
</configtype>
</servcat>
</section></manual></suzuki>
